# The build context is copied into the daemon; keep it to what the image needs.

# 20 GB of build artifacts, and none of them are for the image's platform.
/target

# The local development override. It patches `rainier-framework` to a sibling
# checkout that does not exist inside the container, so a build with this file
# present fails to resolve the dependency. Git ignores it; Docker has to be
# told separately.
/.cargo

# Secrets, and per-developer state. `.env.build` is deliberately **not**
# ignored: it is the selections-only file that sizes the image (see the
# Dockerfile), and it must never hold a credential precisely because it
# travels into the build.
.env
*.sqlite

# The assets stage runs `npm ci` itself; the context needs the lockfile, not
# the tree. `public/build` is built inside the image; a local build (or a
# stale `public/hot`) must not leak in.
node_modules
public/build
public/hot
*.sqlite-journal
/storage/logs/*
/storage/mail/*

/.git
/.github
/.idea
/.vscode
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
